<title>USA: Cairn reserves rise 38 percent.</title>
<headline>Cairn reserves rise 38 percent.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cairn Energy USA Inc said on Monday that its estimated proved oil and gas reserves at December 31, 1996, increased over 38 percent to 111.4 billion cubic feet of gas equivalent from 80.6 billion cubic feet.</p>
<p>The company said its production replacement in 1996 exceeded 350 percent.</p>
<p>Cairn's proven reserves total 82.0 billion cubic feet of gas and 4.9 million barrels of oil, it said.</p>
<p>The company cited its participation in 21 wells -- of which 11 were successful -- in the Gulf of Mexico as a source of increased reserves.</p>
</text>
